      source: "Photograph of Osamu Tezuka from the Asahi Graph issue of 10 June 1953, credited to the Asahi Shimbun company, scanned and hosted on Wikimedia Commons as 'Tezuka Osamu.JPG'. Rights basis: published in Japan in 1953, before 1 January 1958, so public domain in Japan under the transitional rule for old photographs and therefore public domain in the United States (Japanese copyright expired before the 1996 restoration date); Commons tags it as an old-photograph public-domain file with no US-restoration warning. Same basis as the Asahi Graph photograph used for another Japanese subject in this roster. Saved at the Commons original size of 407 x 467, no resizing and no upscaling. Caveat: the individual photographer is not named, and the basis depends on the 1953 publication date given on the file page, which I could not check against the magazine itself. The Wikidata lead (a 1951 photograph, 595 x 508, unknown author) was rejected because its only source is a 1989 book and no earlier publication is documented.",
